@call c09 seizure start=13:27:15
@patient age=23 sex=male weight_kg=70 complaint="shaking episode, still seizing on arrival" allergies=NKDA home_meds="Keppra" history="epilepsy, missed doses"
@traps status epilepticus
RD: Medic 8, seizure, twenty-three year old male, at the gym.  >> dispatch:seizure "seizure"
GAP 3
M1: Medic 8 on scene.  >> time:eTimes.06 "on scene"
GAP 2
BY: He's been shaking for like five minutes. He has epilepsy, he takes Keppra, but he said he ran out.
M1: Still seizing. Protect his head. Get him on his side.  >> status:actively seizing "Still seizing"
TAP knock +label
M2: Sat's 86, heart rate 132.  >> vital:spo2=86 "Sat's 86"; vital:hr=132 "heart rate 132"
M1: Nasal cannula... no, non-rebreather, 15.  >> med:oxygen,15,,NRB "non-rebreather, 15"
GAP 2
TAP button +label
M1: Versed 10 milligrams IM, left deltoid.  >> med:midazolam,10,mg,IM "Versed 10 milligrams IM"
GAP 12
TAP snap -
GAP 12
M2: Seizure stopped. He's postictal, snoring respirations.  >> status:postictal "He's postictal"
M1: NPA, right nare.  >> proc:NPA "NPA"
GAP 4
TAP button +label
M2: Sugar 104. BP 146 over 90, resps 16.  >> vital:bgl=104 "Sugar 104"; vital:bp=146/90 "BP 146 over 90"; vital:rr=16 "resps 16"
GAP 6
M2: Sat's coming up, 95.  >> vital:spo2=95 "95"
GAP 5
M1: Transporting to County.  >> time:eTimes.09 "Transporting"
GAP 10
M2: GCS is 10. Eyes open to voice.  >> vital:gcs=10 "GCS is 10"
GAP 8
M1: Arrived at County.  >> time:eTimes.11 "Arrived at County"
GAP 12
TAP knock +label
M1: Report given, transfer of care.  >> time:eTimes.12 "transfer of care"
KNOCK3
